35,2,1,talk,Kenji,,It's bad. Our yards are a mess of old gear and we can't afford a blackout during peak season.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"My findings confirm it. Capital is cut, but operating costs creep up. We cannot afford modular pricing that climbs yearly.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"We have a disaster waiting. Support is fragmented across vendors, and our ""frozen"" scopes never survive a year.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Rin,,"We've been skipping upgrades because we're too scared to test, and external data moves left us with errors for years.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"We are losing our experts to retirement, and the depot crews simply ignore trainers who don't understand their routines.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Servas, if the crews ignore trainers, we need someone who actually stays on-site to help them.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Asuka, if support is scattered, we need a single point of accountability, not a collection of separate licenses.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"Exactly. A fixed configuration might be better than ""flexible"" workflows that just lead to scope creep.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Rin,,"And we need a system that doesn't require a massive, risky data lift every few years.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,I agree. A partner who understands the grit of the depot floor is more valuable than a fancy feature list.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Rin, does that mean we should avoid the cloud if it means more external dependencies?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"Not necessarily, but we must avoid the ""add-on"" trap where the bill grows every month.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"I'm leaning toward a vendor that provides a rigid, hosted suite to prevent the fragmentation I saw.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Rin,,As long as it doesn't age in place like our current dispatch tool.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"We must prioritize the people. If the administrators are gone, the vendor must fill that gap.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
