60,3,1,talk,Kenji,,Candidate C has an engineering team present through rollout. That's exactly what the depots need.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Candidate C is on our own servers, which means maintenance instead of climbing subscription fees. I like that.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Candidate D has a fixed configuration process. That solves my fear of the plan drifting from the business.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Rin,,"Candidate A uses a partner for migration, but I'm worried about the ""external team"" pattern I found.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,Candidate C's on-site team would support the supervisors and fill the gap left by retiring administrators.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Asuka, D is hosted, but will they survive a peak-season cutover without being here in person?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Rin, Candidate B's modular licensing is exactly the ""yearly climb"" I want to avoid.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Kenji, that's a fair point. D's regional team isn't the same as C's on-site engineering team.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Rin,,"Candidate C is built specifically for transport. It might avoid the ""general tool"" failure of 2021.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,The presence of the engineering team in Candidate C is the most compassionate choice for our exhausted staff.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'm voting for C. It's the only one that feels like it respects the yard.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,I agree. The cost structure of C is the most predictable for the board.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"I'm torn, but the accountability of an on-site team in C outweighs the fixed process of D.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Rin,,"C avoids the external data lift risks and the ""generalist"" software trap. I'm in.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,My heart and mind are with C. It supports the people who do the work.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
